WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.390
- All right y'all, I'm back with

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.464
Jason Derulo and Nicole Byer!

00:00:03.464 --> 00:00:06.010
(audience cheers)

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:09.110
And we're helping Emily who
says she's unlucky in love

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:11.460
and finds all the wrong prospects online.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.100
Well, today things are gonna change.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.330
We're trying a new approach
with Emily, all right?

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:17.160
She's borrowing my chair from "The Voice"

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.710
to pick her next man.

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.650
She'll have no idea
what the guys look like

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.060
because this chair forces you to listen.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.953
This is "Blind Dating".

00:00:24.953 --> 00:00:27.720
(audience cheers)

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.688
All right, let's meet the guys.

00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:32.521
(audience cheers)

00:00:34.966 --> 00:00:38.930
All right, so go ahead guys,
y'all introduce yourselves.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:42.191
- Hi everybody, my name is Tim, hi Emily.

00:00:42.191 --> 00:00:43.024
- Hello.

00:00:43.024 --> 00:00:45.520
- I come from a small farm town
called Almont, Michigan but,

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.460
I live out here in Los Angeles
as a independent film maker.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.568
- [Kelly] Awesome, okay!

00:00:51.568 --> 00:00:52.930
(audience applause)

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:54.380
- Hi Emily, I'm Nick.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.340
I'm from Miami, Florida, I
speak five languages, French,

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:01.123
Portuguese, Spanish, German.
- Oh my gosh, slacker!

00:01:02.056 --> 00:01:03.310
(audience applause)

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:04.790
So, here's how this is gonna go.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:07.170
Tim and Nick will take turns talking.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.330
Just like in "The Voice", if
Emily hears something she likes

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.650
she'll hit the button.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.220
The chair will turn and that
will be the man she chooses.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.140
While she can hit the button at any time,

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.846
it doesn't mean she should.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.040
(laughter)

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.330
This works better with
just a little patience,

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:24.240
let's get started.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.193
Tim and Nick, what is your
idea of a perfect date?

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:30.140
- Well, my idea of a perfect
date actually involves

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.164
the happiest place of Earth, Disneyland.

00:01:33.164 --> 00:01:34.040
(audience cheers)

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.930
I think you get to know
a lot about a person

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.354
by their favorite character and
also what rides they choose.

00:01:39.354 --> 00:01:40.187
- Yes.

00:01:40.187 --> 00:01:42.660
- So, we would start of the day
by walking down Main Street,

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.990
maybe sharing a churro,
some ice cream maybe,

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.450
and then we would have
a reservation for two

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.520
at one of their five star restaurants,

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.510
and then finish off the evening

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:53.950
with a beautiful firework
show at Cinderella's Castle.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.150
- All right, he knows what's
happening there, all right.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.807
Panel, what do you guys think?

00:01:57.807 --> 00:01:59.219
- No, no!

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.260
- No?
- No!

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.469
That's too magical, the second
date is what, in a dumpster?

00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:05.550
(laughter)

00:02:05.550 --> 00:02:06.919
You can only go down from there.

00:02:06.919 --> 00:02:07.752
- [Kelly] It's gonna go down from there.

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:10.530
- But, I also feel like the
answer was a little like,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.363
let me give her what she wants.

00:02:11.363 --> 00:02:12.880
- No, no, no, I will tell you this.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.270
I read things they were gonna
say before they got here,

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.227
he actually had that in his
thing before he came here.

00:02:18.227 --> 00:02:19.750
- Oh!
- What, wow!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:22.160
- He actually had that, that was not

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:23.620
because he heard us talking.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:24.453
- I thought the same thing.

00:02:24.453 --> 00:02:25.602
- You thought that too?

00:02:25.602 --> 00:02:26.435
- I kinda did, yeah.

00:02:26.435 --> 00:02:27.750
- Yeah, yeah, no.
- I'm glad we cleared that up.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:28.890
- All right, good job.
- All right, so Nick,

00:02:28.890 --> 00:02:30.380
what's your perfect date?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.820
- Well, I would be taking you

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:36.210
to the second happiest place
on Earth, Runyon Canyon.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:39.580
We'd go hiking 'cause I'm very adventurous

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:41.470
and we'd go up to the top, right?

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.210
Get to know each other a little bit.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:46.370
See the sunset, watch the LA lights,

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.180
and I'd take you to my favorite
Michelin star restaurant.

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.600
- All right, all right.
- Damn, okay, they got money!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.860
- That's two dates in one!

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:53.693
- [Nicole] That's money!

00:02:53.693 --> 00:02:55.080
- [Jason] That's spending
the whole day together

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:55.913
A day date.
- What do you think

00:02:55.913 --> 00:02:57.378
about hiking on the first date guys?

00:02:57.378 --> 00:02:58.810
- I'm not going hiking,
you can't get to know me

00:02:58.810 --> 00:02:59.763
while I'm huffing and puffing.

00:02:59.763 --> 00:03:01.346
(laughter)

00:03:01.346 --> 00:03:04.170
- [Kelly] Actually, I'm like
so in, I'm easy to please.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.850
I'm like, that sounds fun.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:06.683
- No.

00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:08.350
- Yeah, you know though,
you know I like about it,

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:11.674
if you like me sweaty and
gross, then you're in.

00:03:11.674 --> 00:03:12.507
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:12.507 --> 00:03:13.340
- You know what I'm saying?

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:14.339
Yeah, I'm showing you the worst.

00:03:14.339 --> 00:03:15.172
(audience applause)

00:03:15.172 --> 00:03:17.360
- [Jason] No, I like that
one, I like that one.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.852
- All right, well you like
working out, so, yeah.

00:03:18.852 --> 00:03:19.685
- Yeah, I do.

00:03:19.685 --> 00:03:21.620
- All right, well great job guys.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.828
You haven't hit the button, Emily.

00:03:22.828 --> 00:03:24.570
Yeah, you're, okay, okay good.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:25.557
Let's ramp things up.
- I'm being patient.

00:03:25.557 --> 00:03:28.180
- You know I believe in the magic of song.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:30.685
And this is my "Voice" chair,
so I just embarrass these men.

00:03:30.685 --> 00:03:31.684
(laughter)

00:03:31.684 --> 00:03:33.660
So, I asked Tim and Nick to pen

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.130
they're very own love ballads.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:37.000
All right guys, it's all on you.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.420
Emily, you hit the button if you feel it.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.930
But, maybe listen to both songs, okay.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.890
